class:: PulsarXPM
summary:: A bandlimited pulsar oscillator with cross-phase modulation and oversampling
categories:: UGens>Oscillator

DESCRIPTION::
PulsarXPM is a bandlimited pulsar oscillator with cross-phase modulation and optional oversampling. 
It supports up to 8 simultaneously active grains with internal voice allocation.

Sub-sample-accurate event scheduling of grains can be achieved by combining PulsarXPM with SchedulerCycle, SchedulerBurst or SchedulerBank, 
which provide the necessary timing information (trigger, rate, and subsample offset).

Each grain consists of two cross-phase-modulated wavetable oscillators shaped by an envelope wavetable oscillator. 
The oscillators modulate each other’s phase through a single-sample feedback loop, 
with independent modulation indices controlling the depth of each cross-modulation path. 
Each path includes a slope-tracking lowpass filter whose cutoff follows the modulator’s fundamental frequency 
and is controlled by the corresponding damping parameter.
The wavetable oscillators are bandlimited via dynamic mipmapping and sinc interpolation.

Grains can be overlapped by dividing the scheduler rate by the desired overlap amount before passing it as the trigger frequency. 
An overlap of 1 means each grain lasts exactly one trigger period, while higher values produce longer, overlapping grains.

note::
High overlap values require more CPU as more grains are active simultaneously.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: trig
Trigger signal, for example derived from SchedulerCycle, SchedulerBurst or SchedulerBank.

ARGUMENT:: triggerFreq
Trigger frequency in Hz, for example derived from SchedulerCycle, SchedulerBurst or SchedulerBank.
Used by the internal voice allocator to calculate the grain duration.
Typically the scheduler rate divided by the overlap amount.

ARGUMENT:: subSampleOffset
Subsample offset for accurate grain timing, for example derived from SchedulerCycle, SchedulerBurst or SchedulerBank.

ARGUMENT:: oscFreq
Carrier oscillator frequency in Hz. Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: modFreq
Modulator oscillator frequency in Hz. Latched per grain trigger.

ARGUMENT:: oscPmIndex
Phase modulation depth received by osc from mod.

ARGUMENT:: modPmIndex
Phase modulation depth received by mod from osc.

ARGUMENT:: oscPmDamping
Damping of the phase modulation path from mod to osc.

ARGUMENT:: modPmDamping
Damping of the phase modulation path from osc to mod.

ARGUMENT:: oscBufNum
Buffer containing carrier wavetable data (the size has to be a power-of-2).

ARGUMENT:: oscNumCycles
Number of cycles in the carrier wavetable buffer.

ARGUMENT:: oscCyclePos
Position within the carrier multi-cycle wavetable.

ARGUMENT:: modBufNum
Buffer containing modulator wavetable data (the size has to be a power-of-2).

ARGUMENT:: modNumCycles
Number of cycles in the modulator wavetable buffer.

ARGUMENT:: modCyclePos
Position within the modulator multi-cycle wavetable.

ARGUMENT:: envBufNum
Buffer containing envelope wavetable data (the size has to be a power-of-2).

ARGUMENT:: envNumCycles
Number of cycles in the envelope wavetable buffer.

ARGUMENT:: envCyclePos
Position within the envelope multi-cycle wavetable.

ARGUMENT:: oversample
Oversampling factor: 0=1x, 1=2x, 2=4x, 3=8x, 4=16x.

returns:: Audio-rate UGen.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Create multi-cycle wavetable
(
t = Signal.sineFill(2048, [1], [0]);
u = Signal.sineFill(2048, 1.0/((1..512)**2)*([1,0,-1,0]!128).flatten);
w = Signal.sineFill(2048, 1.0/(1..512)*([1,0]!256).flatten);
x = Signal.sineFill(2048, 1.0/(1..512));
v = t.addAll(u).addAll(w).addAll(x);
b = Buffer.loadCollection(s, v);
)

// Create single-cycle envelope
(
e = Buffer.alloc(s, 2048);
e.loadCollection(Signal.hanningWindow(2048));
)

(
{
	var events, sig;

	events = SchedulerCycle.ar(\tFreq.kr(100));

	sig = PulsarXPM.ar(

		trig: events[\trigger],
		triggerFreq: events[\rate] / \overlap.kr(1),
		subSampleOffset: events[\subSampleOffset],

		oscFreq: 440,
		modFreq: 440,

		oscPmIndex: 5,
		modPmIndex: 2,
		oscPmDamping: 0.5,
		modPmDamping: 1,

        oscBufNum: b,
        oscNumCycles: 4,
        oscCyclePos: 0,

        modBufNum: b,
        modNumCycles: 4,
        modCyclePos: 0,

        envBufNum: e,
		envNumCycles: 1,
		envCyclePos: 0,

		oversample: 1,
	);

	sig = LeakDC.ar(sig);
	sig! 2 * 0.1;
}.play;
)
::
